			"notes": "# HBM NTM: Unofficial NeoForge Edition 0.0.2-A\n\n## Added\n\n- Added the first functional implementation of the NTM fluid system.\n- Added Multi Fluid Identifier support.\n- Added configurable fluid types for ducts and fluid storage.\n- Added Universal Infinite Fluid Barrel behavior.\n- Added fluid tank multiblock functionality.\n- Added dynamic fluid coloring for Universal Fluid Ducts.\n- Added Painted Coated Universal Fluid Duct support.\n- Added additional HBM decorative blocks.\n- Added Steel Scaffold.\n- Added additional Anvil functionality and construction recipes.\n- Added original-style Blast Furnace.\n- Added additional HBM furnace fuels.\n- Added Coal, Lignite and Wood Briquettes.\n- Added Ukrainian localization for supported blocks and items.\n- Added radiation shielding support for Reinforced Glass and Reinforced Glass Panes.\n\n## Fluid System\n\n- Reworked Universal Fluid Duct rendering using CE pipe geometry.\n- Added directional duct connection models.\n- Replaced thousands of fluid-specific models with dynamic fluid tinting.\n- Greatly reduced startup model loading time.\n- Removed fluid type from the huge BlockState model matrix.\n- Fluid types are now stored and synchronized through block entities.\n- Added fluid-specific duct overlays.\n- Fixed fluid storage retaining its selected fluid type while empty.\n- Fixed Infinite Fluid Barrel supplying the fluid requested by the connected network.\n- Fixed fluid tank duct connection positions.\n- Restored CE-style 2D duct inventory icons.\n- Improved Painted Coated Universal Fluid Duct rendering.\n\n## Anvil\n\n- Fixed Anvil recipe tier restrictions.\n- Iron Anvil is Tier 1.\n- Steel Anvil is Tier 2.\n- Tier 2 recipes now require Steel Anvil or higher.\n- Fixed JEI always displaying Iron Anvil regardless of recipe tier.\n- JEI now displays Steel Anvil for Tier 2 recipes.\n- Fixed JEI only displaying the first two ingredients of construction recipes.\n- JEI now displays all `extra_inputs`.\n- Fixed multi-input construction recipe display.\n- Fixed Anvil recipe GUI layout.\n- Fixed overflowing Anvil GUI text.\n- Added/fixed stamp progression recipes.\n- Restored the original Assembly Machine Anvil recipe:\n  - 4 Glass\n  - 8 Steel Ingots\n  - 8 Red Copper Ingots\n  - 2 Motors\n  - 4 Vacuum Tube Circuits\n- Assembly Machine Anvil recipe now requires Tier 2.\n- Assembly Machine internal recipes remain separate from its construction recipe.\n\n## Machines\n\n- Restored the original-style Blast Furnace implementation.\n- Restored original Blast Furnace GUI.\n- Added original-style Blast Furnace processing recipes.\n- Added HBM fuel support through the NeoForge furnace fuel system.\n- Fixed Press item visualization.\n- Fixed Red Copper Wire processing.\n- Fixed several Press recipe/material mappings.\n- Fixed Soldering Station model placement and rotation.\n- Soldering Station model now stays aligned with its multiblock footprint when rotated.\n\n## Blocks\n\n- Steel Scaffold now rotates depending on placement direction.\n- Fixed Steel Scaffold model positioning.\n- Fixed Reinforced Glass transparency.\n- Fixed Reinforced Glass Pane connections and edge rendering.\n- Added missing pane `noside` model states.\n- Added radiation resistance to reinforced glass blocks.\n- Fixed Sliding Seal Door model placement.\n- Fixed Sliding Seal Door collision and selection shapes.\n- Fixed Cage Lamp floor, wall and ceiling orientation.\n- Restored original Cage Lamp OBJ geometry.\n- Fixed Cage Lamp emissive appearance.\n- Added multiple decorative HBM/CE blocks.\n\n## Items & Textures\n\n- Fixed Rare Earth Ore Chunk texture.\n- Restored correct Ring Coil texture.\n- Restored High-Speed Steel Bolt coloring.\n- Fixed Overdrive Upgrade Mk2 and Mk3 models/textures.\n- Fixed battery GUI rendering.\n- Fixed Hazmat Cloth ingredients.\n- Fixed several missing or incorrect HBM item textures.\n\n## Rendering & Models\n\n- Fixed multiple OBJ material assignments.\n- Fixed invisible OBJ models caused by missing materials.\n- Fixed old HBM OBJ coordinate offsets.\n\n..."
		},
